In the patch, tumor tissue appears as densely packed, irregular cellular clusters with enlarged, variably shaped nuclei, prominent nucleoli, and scant to moderate cytoplasm; stroma ranges from fibrous to myxoid, with variable mitotic figures and necrotic foci.
tumor tissue displays a dense cellular patch with irregular sheets and nests of pleomorphic, hyperchromatic nuclei, variable nuclear sizes, frequent mitotic figures, occasional necrotic debris, and heterogeneous stromal reactions ranging from fibrosis to edematous change.
Tumor tissue appears as densely packed, irregular cell clusters replacing normal nodal architecture, with variable cell size, pleomorphic hyperchromatic nuclei, scant cytoplasm, frequent mitotic figures, necrotic foci, and invasive, irregular margins.
In lymph node WSI patches, tumor tissue appears as hypercellular, irregular sheets or nests of pleomorphic cells with enlarged vesicular nuclei, conspicuous nucleoli, variable mitoses; variation 4 often shows extensive necrosis and pronounced stromal fibrosis.
In lymph node WSI patches tumor tissue appears as dense cellular aggregates forming sheets, nests, or trabeculae with enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei, variable cytoplasm, frequent mitoses, focal necrosis, and accompanying fibrous stromal reaction.
Tumor tissue patch shows densely packed cells forming irregular nests and sheets within lymphoid stroma, with variable nuclear pleomorphism, coarse chromatin, prominent nucleoli, frequent mitotic figures, focal necrosis, and occasional stromal desmoplasia (variation 6).
tumor tissue in a lymph node WSI patch shows densely packed pleomorphic cells forming irregular nests and sheets, varying nuclear size and chromatin density, scattered mitotic figures, focal necrosis, and variable fibrous stroma.
In lymph node WSI tumor patches, tissue often appears as densely packed pleomorphic cells forming irregular sheets and glands with variable nuclear size, coarse chromatin, frequent mitotic figures, focal necrosis, and heterogeneous stromal fibrosis or inflammation.
tumor tissue appears as irregularly shaped nests and cords of densely packed cells replacing nodal architecture, with variable nuclear pleomorphism, hyperchromasia, occasional necrotic foci, mitotic figures, and desmoplastic stromal reactions across patches.
shows dense cellular sheets with variable cell size, pleomorphic hyperchromatic nuclei, occasional prominent nucleoli and mitoses, interspersed necrotic pale areas, fibrous stroma and hemorrhage, with heterogeneous basophilic and eosinophilic staining.
